Pros: Good graphics;
You need to make every shot count as there are limited supplies;
Can get infected if bitten by a zombie. When the player turns, He will attack the human players;
The only HUD you have is: ammo (Opcional), Objectives and compass;
Melee combat is decent. Your character has limited Stamina, so you have to manage stamina as best as possible;
It has good connections online;
On objective mode, it randomizes objectives for each time you start on the same map.
Cons: Zombie Spawns can get you cornered easily, making almost impossible to not die.
Even with the nerfs, the machete is still Overpowerd;
Some guns have ridiculously low fire rate;
Carrying quest items such as, a key, you have to hold it on your face, literally, and you are unable to run and attack, but you can jump.

Eidolon is a game that has a lot of rough edges both figuratively and literally, but IF you just want a well-crafted nature exploration game one in a beautiful place to escape and zone out for a while consider this game. It even adds a survival mechanic to make what would otherwise be a walking sim more engaging.
